---
/**
 * woodworks / PageBV — "Narra & Co." (solid-wood furniture makers).
 *
 * Linen and walnut: Young Serif display over Work Sans body on a warm linen
 * ground, a rust accent, and dark walnut bands (the marquee strip, the custom
 * commission slab, the how-it-works band, the footer and the hero spec card)
 * carrying tan labels. Sharp-ish 6px controls, 10px plates, no motion.
 *
 * ROLE OF THIS FILE: the wrapper emits the WHOLE document (doctype, head,
 * tokens, fonts, Leaflet boot, skip link). It does NOT compose with
 * BaseLayout. It is the only file in the variant that touches siteData; the
 * sixteen section components (Header and Footer included) receive only
 * layout and content.
 *
 * EDITABLE HOOKS OWNED BY THIS FILE: none. It only READS layout.businessName
 * and layout.tagline (for the title), the content description (meta
 * description), layout.favicon and layout.ogImage. Every data-field,
 * data-image-field and data-href-field hook lives in a section component.
 * Section visibility is the camelCase visibility keys below, each tested
 * with !== false (undefined renders).
 *
 * HARDCODED VISIBLE STRINGS: none of them is content. The skip link's "Skip
 * to content" below (an a11y affordance, visible on focus only), and the
 * fixed structural labels, each rendered only beside an owner value:
 * Address / Hours / Phone in LocationBV's ledger and the Follow heading in
 * FooterBV (drawn only over a real social link). Nothing else is literal.
 *
 * PROP PLUMBING: every section is handed BOTH content and layout, even the
 * ones that read only content. Extra props are inert in Astro.
 *
 * DESIGN ISOLATION: every selector in the global block is prefixed
 * html[data-page="BV"], including the box-sizing reset, body, img, a,
 * ::selection and the base primitives, because index.astro bundles every
 * wrapper's global CSS onto every customer page.
 *
 * TOKEN PLAN (THE DESIGN IS THE SPECIFICATION; every native value is lifted
 * verbatim from "Woodworks BV - Narra.dc.html"):
 *   roles the engine may move, so an admin colour pick recolours coherently
 *     ground #EFE6D8 is --paper; the oatmeal band #E4D7C3 is --paper-2; the
 *     card #F7F1E7 is --card; text #2A1D14 is --ink; the muted brown #5E4E40
 *     is --ink-soft; the rust #8A3B1E is --accent-deep when it is TEXT on a
 *     light ground (eyebrows, stars, the FAQ plus, the directions rule) and
 *     --accent only where nothing reads it (the logo rings, the map pin).
 *     Natively they are the same rust; under a scheme the engine maps them
 *     to primaryDeep and primary, and the deep one is the text-safe tone.
 *   the rust FILL that carries a label
 *     --fill (buttons, the header pill's hover, the closing band, the last
 *     how step, the message pill, ::selection) under an --on-primary label
 *     (#FFF5EA natively; the engine's pickOn(primary) under a scheme). It is
 *     var(--accent) natively and under any scheme whose primary holds 4.5:1
 *     against --on-primary (brown, dark, black). Where it does not (the
 *     engine's 0.5 luminance threshold puts WHITE on orange 2.80:1, gold
 *     2.46:1, green 3.30:1) the scheme node below re-points it to the deep
 *     primary, and, where even that is short (gold, 3.84:1), to the deep
 *     primary taken toward the label's opposite in 10% steps until it holds
 *     4.5:1 — computed at build time from the engine's own values.
 *   the tone that faces a fill
 *     --fill-alt: the walnut the fill hovers to and the header pill's resting
 *     fill, always under a --paper label. var(--ink) natively; where the
 *     scheme's fill IS its ink (green's deep primary is its ink, black's
 *     primary is its ink) the hover would be invisible, so the node points it
 *     at --ink-soft, which the engine pairs with --paper.
 *   the FIXED WOOD WORLD the engine does not know, deliberately
 *     --wood #2A1D14, --wood-2 #3D2B1F, --on-wood #EFE6D8 and --tan #D9A77F.
 *     The walnut bands ARE the design (the PageBJ precedent for its green):
 *     an admin pick recolours paper, ink and rust around them and the bands
 *     stay walnut with linen text and tan labels, which is legible in every
 *     scheme because none of those four tokens can move.
 *   two soft labels on the rust fill
 *     --on-accent-2 #FFE9DA (body copy) and --on-accent-3 #EFE6D8 (the last
 *     step's title). They cannot be derived from --on-primary by mixing, so
 *     they are native tokens, re-pointed to --on-primary by the small style
 *     node gated on an explicit scheme below (never on the override CSS
 *     merely being non-empty, which a font pick alone makes it).
 *   the About portrait plate
 *     --plate #D6C6AE, the design's plate one step darker than the oatmeal
 *     band; under a scheme the node mixes it from --paper-2 and --ink, so the
 *     plate keeps its relation to whatever band it sits on.
 *
 * FONT-PAIRING SENTINEL (verbatim from PageBJ): lib/astro-builder.ts defaults
 * layout.fontPairing to the literal 'modern' and lockVariant only blanks
 * ''/'auto'/'default', so without the sentinel buildOverrideCss would
 * force-swap Space Grotesk + Inter onto nearly every real site. 'modern' is
 * treated as unset; a deliberate admin pick still applies.
 *
 * FORBIDDEN CLASS NAMES (lib/genericThemeOverrides.ts pins them):
 *   .btn-primary .btn-ghost .btn-yellow .btn-light .nav-cta .nav-right
 *   .testi .cta-band .trust, and hero as a class on any element.
 * Buttons here are .btn--fill / .btn--line / .linkc plus section-scoped
 * modifiers; the footer carries no .btn at all (it would inherit the
 * engine's footer label pin) and the message pill is a sibling after it.
 *
 * RENDER ORDER, exactly as the design draws it: Header, Hero (#top), Marquee
 * (#marquee), Trust, Services (#services), About (#about), Why (#why), How
 * (#how), Gallery (#gallery), Testimonials (#reviews), Credentials
 * (#credentials), Area (#area), Faq (#faq), Location (#visit) inside main,
 * then the closing band (#book), the Footer and the floating message pill.
 *
 * NO MOTION: the design has no reveal, no marquee scroll and no hover
 * transition, so none is added. Smooth anchor scrolling is the design's own
 * and is switched off under prefers-reduced-motion.
 *
 * Leaflet: this wrapper loads leaflet.css and leaflet.js and defines
 * window.__woodworksBVInitMap (family-unique). LocationBV calls that exact
 * name. Keep el.innerHTML = '' in the boot (it erases the drawn fallback
 * face) and keep id="map" literal.
 */
import HeaderBV from './header/HeaderBV.astro';
import HeroBV from './hero/HeroBV.astro';
import MarqueeBV from './marquee/MarqueeBV.astro';
import TrustBV from './trust/TrustBV.astro';
import ServicesBV from './services/ServicesBV.astro';
import AboutBV from './about/AboutBV.astro';
import WhyBV from './why/WhyBV.astro';
import HowBV from './how/HowBV.astro';
import GalleryBV from './gallery/GalleryBV.astro';
import TestimonialsBV from './testimonials/TestimonialsBV.astro';
import CredentialsBV from './credentials/CredentialsBV.astro';
import AreaBV from './area/AreaBV.astro';
import FaqBV from './faq/FaqBV.astro';
import LocationBV from './location/LocationBV.astro';
import CtaBandBV from './ctaBand/CtaBandBV.astro';
import FooterBV from './footer/FooterBV.astro';
import { resolveTheme, buildFontHref, buildOverrideCss } from '../../lib/genericThemeOverrides';

interface Props { siteData: any; }
const { siteData } = Astro.props;
const layout = siteData.layout ?? {};
const content = siteData.content ?? {};
const visibility = siteData.visibility ?? {};
const title = layout.businessName
  ? `${layout.businessName}${layout.tagline ? ' — ' + layout.tagline : ''}`
  : 'Welcome';
const { scheme: __themeScheme, pairing: __resolvedPairing } = resolveTheme(layout, (content as any).business_type, { lockVariant: true });
// 'modern' is astro-builder's DEFAULT, not a choice (lib/astro-builder.ts).
// Treating it as unset keeps Young Serif + Work Sans; a deliberate pick applies.
const __themePairing = __resolvedPairing === 'modern' ? '' : __resolvedPairing;
const __overrideCss = buildOverrideCss(__themeScheme, __themePairing);
const __fontHref = buildFontHref(__themePairing);
// THE SCHEME NODE. Gated on an explicit scheme that actually produced a
// palette (the engine block then carries --paper), never on the override CSS
// merely being non-empty: a font pick alone fills it too.
//   · the two soft labels on the rust fill have no engine equivalent, so they
//     follow --on-primary, the engine's own label for its primary;
//   · the About plate is mixed from the scheme's band and ink;
//   · the FILL (see the doc comment) is chosen from the engine's OWN values,
//     read back out of its override block: primary if it holds 4.5:1 under
//     --on-primary, else the deep primary, else the deep primary taken toward
//     the label's opposite in 10% steps until it does;
//   · --fill-alt leaves --ink when the chosen fill is (nearly) the ink itself.
// SPECIFICITY, not source order: Astro hoists the global block below into the
// bundled stylesheet at the END of the document, while this set:html node
// stays inline in the head — so a plain html[data-page] rule here would lose
// the tie to the native tokens. The extra :root makes it (0,2,1).
const __schemePicked = Boolean(__themeScheme) && /--paper:/.test(__overrideCss);
const __hex = (name: string): string => {
  const m = new RegExp(`--${name}:\\s*#([0-9a-fA-F]{6})\\b`).exec(__overrideCss);
  return m ? m[1].toUpperCase() : '';
};
const __rgb = (h: string): number[] => [0, 2, 4].map((k) => parseInt(h.slice(k, k + 2), 16));
const __lum = (h: string): number => {
  const [r, g, b] = __rgb(h).map((c) => {
    const s = c / 255;
    return s <= 0.03928 ? s / 12.92 : ((s + 0.055) / 1.055) ** 2.4;
  });
  return 0.2126 * r + 0.7152 * g + 0.0722 * b;
};
const __ratio = (a: string, b: string): number => {
  const x = __lum(a);
  const y = __lum(b);
  return (Math.max(x, y) + 0.05) / (Math.min(x, y) + 0.05);
};
const __toward = (h: string, to: number, t: number): string =>
  __rgb(h).map((c) => Math.round(c + (to - c) * t).toString(16).padStart(2, '0')).join('').toUpperCase();
let __fillFix = '';
if (__schemePicked) {
  const primary = __hex('accent');
  const deep = __hex('accent-deep');
  const onPrimary = __hex('on-primary');
  const ink = __hex('ink');
  if (primary && deep && onPrimary && ink) {
    let fill = primary;
    if (__ratio(primary, onPrimary) < 4.5) {
      fill = deep;
      const to = __lum(onPrimary) > 0.5 ? 0 : 255;
      for (let k = 1; k <= 10 && __ratio(fill, onPrimary) < 4.5; k++) fill = __toward(deep, to, k / 10);
    }
    if (fill !== primary) __fillFix += `--fill:#${fill};`;
    if (__ratio(fill, ink) < 1.25) __fillFix += '--fill-alt:var(--ink-soft);';
  }
}
const __schemeFix = __schemePicked
  ? `html[data-page="BV"]:root{--on-accent-2:var(--on-primary);--on-accent-3:var(--on-primary);--plate:color-mix(in srgb,var(--paper-2) 88%,var(--ink));${__fillFix}}`
  : '';
const __og = layout.ogImage || layout.favicon || '';
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-page="BV">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>{title}</title>
  {content.description && <meta name="description" content={content.description} />}
  <!-- Browser-chrome tint. A meta tag cannot read a CSS var, so this repeats
       the linen ground (--paper) the sticky header sits on. -->
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#EFE6D8" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin="" />
  <!-- The design's own faces, exactly as its helmet link loads them: Young
       Serif (one weight, 400) for display, Work Sans 400-700 for body and
       labels. Always loaded, so the variant reads as designed when the admin
       never touched the font dropdown. -->
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Young+Serif&family=Work+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css" integrity="sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY=" crossorigin="" />
  {layout.favicon && <link rel="icon" href={layout.favicon} />}
  {__og && <meta property="og:image" content={__og} />}

  <style is:global>
    /* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       PageBV · "Narra & Co." — woodworks. Tokens + shared base primitives.
       EVERY selector is prefixed html[data-page="BV"] so nothing leaks into a
       sister wrapper, or in.

       LOAD-BEARING FACTS:
       1. SPECIFICITY. Every appearance-bearing primitive is wrapped in
          :where(), so it scores (0,1,1) and an Astro-scoped section rule
          (0,2,0) always wins. :where() adds ZERO specificity, so if a control
          looks wrong in the full build, suspect a leak from another family.
       2. SOURCE ORDER. The link hover sits BEFORE the button rules: all of
          them score (0,1,1), and a later a:hover would repaint every button
          label rust on hover.
       3. HEAD ORDER. This block is followed by the scheme-gated fix, the
          font-pick link and then, LAST in the head, the engine's override
          node. Astro hoists THIS block into the bundled stylesheet at the end
          of the document, so neither later node can rely on source order: the
          engine wins with !important, the scheme fix with a :root compound.
          (Never write a literal closing style tag inside this block,
          comments included — it is a raw-text element.)
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

    html[data-page="BV"] {
      /* grounds — linen page, oatmeal band, pale card */
      --paper: #EFE6D8;
      --paper-2: #E4D7C3;
      --card: #F7F1E7;
      /* ink — the design's walnut near-black, and its muted brown */
      --ink: #2A1D14;
      --ink-soft: #5E4E40;
      --muted: #5E4E40;
      /* ink at the design's 18% over linen (#CCC2B5). Rules draw hairlines
         as rgba(var(--ink-rgb), alpha) to keep each of the design's alphas. */
      --line: #CCC2B5;
      --stone: #CCC2B5;
      /* rust — TEXT on a light ground is --accent-deep; --accent only where
         nothing reads it (rings, pin); a FILL carrying a label is --fill */
      --accent: #8A3B1E;
      --accent-deep: #8A3B1E;
      /* the labelled rust fill, and the walnut that faces it (hover of a fill,
         the header pill at rest). Engine-unknown names; the scheme node picks
         their values from the engine's own palette (see the frontmatter). */
      --fill: var(--accent);
      --fill-alt: var(--ink);
      --accent-light: #D9A77F;
      --accent-soft: #D9A77F;
      /* rgb triplets for token-driven tints */
      --paper-rgb: 239,230,216;
      --ink-rgb: 42,29,20;
      --accent-rgb: 138,59,30;
      /* contrast aliases the engine and inherited rules expect */
      --on-primary: #FFF5EA;
      --on-accent: #FFF5EA;
      --on-ink: #EFE6D8;
      --on-paper: #2A1D14;
      /* THE FIXED WOOD WORLD. Names the engine does not know, on purpose:
         the walnut bands are the design, and they carry their own linen text
         and tan labels, so no scheme can strand a label on them. */
      --wood: #2A1D14;
      --wood-2: #3D2B1F;
      --on-wood: #EFE6D8;
      --on-wood-rgb: 239,230,216;
      --tan: #D9A77F;
      /* drop shadows stay walnut in every scheme (a white glow under a dark
         scheme's light ink would read as a halo, not a shadow) */
      --shadow-rgb: 42,29,20;
      /* soft labels on the rust fill (see the frontmatter) */
      --on-accent-2: #FFE9DA;
      --on-accent-3: #EFE6D8;
      /* the About portrait plate, one step darker than the oatmeal band */
      --plate: #D6C6AE;
      /* type + metrics */
      --disp: "Young Serif", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
      --serif: "Young Serif", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
      --sans: "Work Sans", system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      /* The design has no monospace; its tracked caps are Work Sans 600. */
      --mono: "Work Sans", system-ui, -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
      --maxw: 1280px;
      --gut: clamp(18px, 4vw, 48px);
    }

    /* VERIFIED CONTRAST (sRGB relative luminance, the design's palette):
       ink/paper 13.22 · ink/card 14.55 · ink/paper-2 11.53
       ink-soft/paper 6.43 · ink-soft/paper-2 5.61 · ink-soft/card 7.08
       rust/paper 6.23 · rust/paper-2 5.43 · rust/card 6.86 (eyebrows, stars)
       on-primary/rust 7.16 (buttons, closing band) · on-accent-2/rust 6.58
       on-wood/wood 13.22 · tan/wood 7.62 · tan/wood-2 6.26 (walnut labels)
       linen at 80% over wood 8.92, over wood-2 7.56 · at 60% (colophon) 5.63
       Every pairing the design draws clears WCAG AA. */

    /* ── reset + document ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BV"] *,
    html[data-page="BV"] *::before,
    html[data-page="BV"] *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html[data-page="BV"] {
      -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;
      /* the design's own html{scroll-behavior:smooth} */
      scroll-behavior: smooth;
      /* The sticky header is 77px (76 + its hairline). One declaration on the
         root covers every in-page anchor, FAQ rows and the map included. */
      scroll-padding-top: 89px;
    }
    /* The fixed message pill (54px, 12-24px off the bottom, up to the full
       width of a phone) would otherwise sit on top of whatever keyboard focus
       scrolls to the viewport's bottom edge (WCAG 2.4.11). Only when the
       pill is actually on the page. */
    html[data-page="BV"]:has(> body > a.pill) { scroll-padding-bottom: 88px; }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { html[data-page="BV"] { scroll-behavior: auto; } }
    html[data-page="BV"] body {
      margin: 0; padding: 0;
      background-color: var(--paper); color: var(--ink);
      font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 17px; font-weight: 400; line-height: 1.65;
      -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; overflow-x: hidden;
    }
    html[data-page="BV"] img { max-width: 100%; display: block; }
    /* Leaflet's own anchors are kept OUT of the reset and the link hover
       (woodworks:BY's rule). Scoped, these would score (0,1,1) — the same as
       leaflet.css `.leaflet-bar a{color:black}` and `.leaflet-container a` —
       and, coming later, win: the zoom glyphs would take --ink, which is
       white under the dark and black schemes, on Leaflet's own white
       buttons. Leaflet's colours are right on Leaflet's fixed chrome. */
    html[data-page="BV"] :where(a:not(.leaflet-container a)) { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
    /* the design's global a:hover{color:#8A3B1E} — BEFORE the buttons (fact 2) */
    html[data-page="BV"] :where(a:not(.leaflet-container a):hover) { color: var(--accent-deep); }
    /* The design's unscoped a:hover also reached the zoom glyphs. Leaflet's
       buttons stay white in every scheme, so their hover is the design's
       literal rust (5.9:1 on Leaflet's #F4F4F4 hover ground), not a token a
       scheme could turn white. */
    html[data-page="BV"] .leaflet-container .leaflet-bar a:not(.leaflet-disabled):hover { color: #8A3B1E; }
    html[data-page="BV"] ::selection { background-color: var(--fill); color: var(--on-primary); }
    /* text-transform is DECLARED, not defaulted: an unscoped uppercase heading
       rule from another template once capitalised every mixed-case design. */
    html[data-page="BV"] :where(h1, h2, h3, h4) {
      margin: 0; font-family: var(--disp); font-weight: 400; color: inherit;
      letter-spacing: 0; text-transform: none;
    }
    html[data-page="BV"] :where(p, figure, blockquote, dl, dd, ol, ul) { margin: 0; }
    html[data-page="BV"] :where(ol, ul) { padding: 0; }
    /* Owner emphasis inside a display heading (headings are set:html, because
       generated headlines may carry <em>). Young Serif ships no italic, so the
       emphasis is the rust, not a synthesised slant. Bands restate it. */
    html[data-page="BV"] :where(h1, h2) :where(em, i) { font-style: normal; color: var(--accent-deep); }

    /* ── layout scaffolding: the design's 1280px container, gutter inside ── */
    html[data-page="BV"] :where(.wrap) {
      max-width: var(--maxw); margin-inline: auto; padding-inline: var(--gut);
    }

    /* ── .kick — the eyebrow: 12px Work Sans 600 caps, .2em, rust ────────── */
    html[data-page="BV"] :where(.kick) {
      margin: 0; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: .2em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent-deep);
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }

    /* ── BUTTONS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
       Straight from the design's style-hover specs:
         .btn--fill  rust fill + rust border, #FFF5EA label -> walnut fill, linen label
                     (--fill -> --fill-alt; see the token plan)
         .btn--line  clear fill, walnut border + label       -> walnut fill, linen label
       Every variant DECLARES its own background-color, and every hover
       restates fill, border AND label, so a label can never strand. No
       transition: the design's hovers are instant. */
    html[data-page="BV"] :where(.btn) {
      background-color: transparent;
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
      min-height: 54px; padding: 0 28px;
      border: 1.5px solid transparent; border-radius: 6px;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: 0; text-transform: none; text-decoration: none; text-align: center;
      cursor: pointer;
    }
    html[data-page="BV"] :where(.btn--fill) {
      background-color: var(--fill); border-color: var(--fill); color: var(--on-primary);
    }
    html[data-page="BV"] :where(.btn--fill:hover) {
      background-color: var(--fill-alt); border-color: var(--fill-alt); color: var(--paper);
    }
    html[data-page="BV"] :where(.btn--line) {
      background-color: transparent; border-color: var(--ink); color: var(--ink);
    }
    html[data-page="BV"] :where(.btn--line:hover) {
      background-color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--ink); color: var(--paper);
    }

    /* ── .linkc — the design's underlined text action (directions) ─────── */
    html[data-page="BV"] :where(.linkc) {
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; min-height: 44px;
      background-color: transparent; color: inherit; font-weight: 600;
      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent-deep);
    }
    html[data-page="BV"] :where(.linkc:hover) { color: var(--accent-deep); }

    /* ── FOCUS · a DUO ring: a linen outline inside a walnut halo, so it reads
          on the linen page (halo) and on every walnut or rust band (outline). */
    html[data-page="BV"] :where(a, button, summary, [tabindex]):focus-visible {
      outline: 3px solid var(--paper); outline-offset: 0;
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 6px var(--ink);
      border-radius: 6px;
    }

    /* ── skip link ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BV"] :where(.skip) {
      position: absolute; left: -999px; top: 0; z-index: 100;
      background-color: var(--ink); color: var(--paper);
      padding: 12px 18px; border-radius: 0 0 6px 0;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600;
    }
    html[data-page="BV"] :where(.skip:focus) { left: 0; top: 0; color: var(--paper); }
  </style>
  {__schemeFix && <style is:global set:html={__schemeFix}></style>}
  {__fontHref && <link href={__fontHref} rel="stylesheet" />}
  <style is:global set:html={__overrideCss}></style>
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
  <HeaderBV layout={layout} content={content} />
  <main id="main">
    {visibility.heroSection !== false && <HeroBV content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.marqueeBlock !== false && <MarqueeBV content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.trustBlock !== false && <TrustBV content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.servicesSection !== false && <ServicesBV content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.aboutSection !== false && <AboutBV content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.whyUsBlock !== false && <WhyBV content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.howItWorksBlock !== false && <HowBV content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.gallerySection !== false && <GalleryBV content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.testimonialsBlock !== false && <TestimonialsBV content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.credentialsBlock !== false && <CredentialsBV content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.serviceAreaBlock !== false && <AreaBV content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.faqBlock !== false && <FaqBV content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.locationBlock !== false && <LocationBV content={content} layout={layout} />}
  </main>
  {visibility.ctaBandBlock !== false && <CtaBandBV content={content} layout={layout} />}
  <FooterBV layout={layout} content={content} />

  <script is:inline src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js" integrity="sha256-20nQCchB9co0qIjJZRGuk2/Z9VM+kNiyxNV1lvTlZBo=" crossorigin=""></script>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      // Narra & Co. / BV Leaflet boot — accepts (lat, lng, label) from
      // LocationBV. The global name is family-unique on purpose: a preview
      // harness can render two wrappers in one document, and a shared name
      // cross-wires the maps.
      window.__woodworksBVInitMap = function (lat, lng, label) {
        if (!window.L) return;
        var el = document.getElementById('map');
        if (!el || el._leaflet_id) return;
        // Erases LocationBV's drawn fallback face; without this the tiles
        // stack on top of the drawn grid.
        el.innerHTML = '';
        var map = L.map('map', { scrollWheelZoom: false }).setView([lat, lng], 15);
        L.tileLayer('https://basemaps.cartocdn.com/rastertiles/voyager/{z}/{x}/{y}{r}.png', {
          attribution: '&copy; OpenStreetMap &copy; CARTO', maxZoom: 19, subdomains: 'abcd'
        }).addTo(map);
        // The design's pin — a 20px rust dot in a linen ring and a walnut
        // hairline — with its colours READ from the live tokens, so an explicit
        // admin colour pick recolours the pin too (the engine sets them on
        // html:root, this same element).
        var cs = window.getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);
        var accent = (cs.getPropertyValue('--accent') || '').trim() || '#8A3B1E';
        var paper = (cs.getPropertyValue('--paper') || '').trim() || '#EFE6D8';
        var ink = (cs.getPropertyValue('--ink') || '').trim() || '#2A1D14';
        var icon = L.divIcon({
          className: '',
          html: '<div style="width:20px;height:20px;border-radius:50%;background:' + accent + ';box-shadow:0 0 0 4px ' + paper + ',0 0 0 5px ' + ink + '"></div>',
          iconSize: [20, 20], iconAnchor: [10, 10]
        });
        L.marker([lat, lng], { icon: icon, title: label || '', keyboard: false }).addTo(map);
      };
    })();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
